2:T449,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Why is it so hard to stop scrolling YouTube Shorts and Instagram Reels?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Short-form video feeds use variable reward schedules—the same neurological trigger behind slot machines. Each swipe releases a micro-dose of dopamine, trapping the brain in an endless novelty-seeking loop."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does PlanBot help curb social media addiction?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"PlanBot replaces unstructured empty time with proactive, color-coded daily focus blocks. When your brain has a clear next task and visual progress streaks, the urge to check Instagram drops significantly."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many hours can I realistically save by time-blocking?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The average smartphone user spends 3.5 to 4.5 hours daily on social media and video apps. Implementing structured AI time-blocking typically reclaims 2 to 3 hours of daily productive focus within the first week."}}]}a:["slug","stop-wasting-time-youtube-instagram-planbot-productivity","d"]
